PLACEHOLDER — REPLACE BEFORE MAKING THE REPOSITORY PUBLIC
=========================================================

No licence has been chosen. Without one, default copyright applies and nobody may legally reuse
the code, which defeats the purpose of releasing it alongside a paper.

For a code-and-data artifact the usual choice is the MIT Licence. GitHub can insert it for you:
Add file -> Create new file -> name it LICENSE -> "Choose a license template" -> MIT, with
"Copyright (c) 2026 Haydar Kilic".

Not covered by whatever licence you choose, and not yours to license:

  * The five UCI datasets used by the real-data controls are not committed here; they are
    downloaded on first use and remain subject to the terms of the UCI Machine Learning
    Repository and of each individual dataset.
